{"kind":"report","text":"CHANGES-REQUESTED at exact clean head e76b508fe97dd75aa549a90b20a160c51287f0a3 on request/refuse-before-signing, governed by Hugh's direct implementation request 9fbb4b216c30e6ffc264d9faf77520a39fd2d3bb. All fifteen named artifacts cover the diff. Four independently reproduced findings prevent the stated conditions from being met.\n\n1. Batch preflight skips the common labeled shape entirely (cmd/gs/preflight.go:224-226). A two-act chain containing a valid assert labeled first, followed by an artifact with body.commit but no body.path and rests_on [\"$first\"], returns success, reports both acts landed, advances depth 9 -\u003e 11, and leaves the artifact ineffective with reason \"artifact state requires body.path\". This is one of Hugh's explicitly named refusal classes, not a race. Preview the ordinary labeled chain against isolated prospective state, using the fold's own rules and resolved prospective references, so the malformed artifact refuses before the first signing/key access or append. Preserve valid labeled chains and the unchanged live projection. Merely documenting that all $label acts escape does not satisfy condition 1.\n\n2. A missing required --kind still reaches the signing key (cmd/gs/main.go:529-555; internal/app/preflight.go:66-68). In a normal fixture, invoke state with --as worker --text \"a fact\" --rests-on \u003cgenesis\u003e --server -, omitting --kind, with worker.key temporarily absent. The result is the key-file open error, with no usage output. Add the required-kind invocation check before workspace/key access and audit the claimed required-argument coverage; verify usage plus example, no key read and no append. This directly violates condition 3 despite the exact-head claim that every malformed signing invocation has been covered.\n\n3. The raw argument scan confuses flag values with flags (cmd/gs/usage.go:105-118). A valid supersede invocation with --text \"--target\" followed by its authorized target is refused as \"gs supersede takes its \u003ctarget-event\u003e as a positional argument, not --target\". The equivalent --text=--target control succeeds. Respect the flag parser's value consumption and end-of-options/positional rules, or classify the actual parse error instead of scanning every raw token. Keep genuine --target mistakes helpful without rejecting valid values.\n\n4. Preflight changes exact retry behavior (cmd/gs/preflight.go:44-47). Ratify a live assert under an explicit idempotency key; let its author supersede it; repeat the identical ratify command and key. The new command refuses \"retired statement cannot be ratified\". Its --no-preflight control replays the original event with no new append. This is a previously accepted act being recovered, not a request to create a new ineffective act. Preserve the accepted-retry path and mismatching-key refusal before judging a fresh act. A documented workaround does not meet the governing outcome that existing behavior on admitted acts is unchanged; this also affects recovery after response loss. Keep new unauthorized acts refused before key access.\n\nArchitecture: layers 5 (workroom decision/Preview), 4 (application composition), and 7 (CLI) are affected. The judge extraction keeps the existing decision path, and the focused preview tests confirm projection immutability and the next append's equivalence for their tested cases. Architecture.md at this head and its candidate artifact record the layer 5/7 additions. The layer 7 claim of unchanged admitted behavior and complete malformed-invocation handling is false for findings 2-4; correct implementation and prose together. No intentional fold rule change or profile bump is needed for this commission.\n\nSecurity: reviewed actor resolution, key-access order, authority checks, prospective state, resident frontier fallback, untrusted CLI/batch inputs and retry identity. No authority grant or signature bypass was found; the fold remains authoritative and --no-preflight does not confer authority. Nevertheless findings 1 and 2 leave the requested pre-signing boundary incomplete. Authority is Hugh's direct request, not an authority-bearing older request chain. Do not weaken submission's identity or idempotency-conflict checks to repair finding 4.\n\nSimplification: keep one shared fold decision path. Cut repeated justification from the new helper comments and consolidate the common preflight explanation across the four reference pages, retaining each command's actual example and differences. Remove the duplicated preflightFixture comment block. This will make the contract easier to assess while the behavioral gaps are repaired.\n\nValidation: supplied focused suite \"go test ./cmd/gs ./internal/workroom -run 'Test(Preflight|MalformedInvocation|EveryCommand|Preview)' -count=1\" passed (cmd/gs 19.045s; workroom 0.290s); diff check passed and checkout stayed clean at the exact head. Independent Go-overlay probes outside the worktree reproduced all four findings. Evidence and reusable fixture probes: /tmp/codex-preflight-e76b508f/overlay.json, probe_test.go and confirmed.txt. Reproduction command: go test -overlay /tmp/codex-preflight-e76b508f/overlay.json ./cmd/gs -run 'TestCodex(ValidFlagValue|MissingKindBeforeKey|BatchLabeledInvalidAct|RetryAfterRetirement)$' -count=1. An exploratory ordered-batch probe was excluded from that command because its --no-preflight baseline also refused; it is not a finding. I did not rerun the author-reported full 36-package suite after these focused failures.\n\nKeep the corrections on the existing implementation commitment. Publish all corrected exact-head artifacts citing this verdict and request fresh independent review.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:9cab89424da0f37301d3002be3f6b00f653d125d","head":"e76b508fe97dd75aa549a90b20a160c51287f0a3","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:26ce78864dc7b25b107d30